From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add a driver for the Sony IMX374

The Sony IMX374 is the front camera sensor of the Samsung Galaxy Z Flip3
(SM-F711N). It sends 10-bit Bayer data over a four-lane MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY
link and is controlled over I2C at 0x1a, with the chip ID 0x0374 at
0x0016.

No datasheet was available. The init list and the three mode lists are
copied from the sensor module that the phone's stock camera stack loads
(com.samsung.sensormodule.12_sony_imx374), in its order and with its
values; only comments were added. Both stock front camera modules carry
the same init list. The modes are:

- 3648x2736, the full 4:3 field, 30 fps, 1818 Mbps per lane
- 1824x1368, the same field binned 2x2, 30 fps, 1794 Mbps per lane
- 1988x1120, a 16:9 field binned 2x2, 30 fps, 798 Mbps per lane

Each mode list programs its own OP PLL, so the link frequency (909, 897
or 399 MHz) follows the mode, and a mode is offered only when its link
frequency is listed in the firmware node. 909 MHz is the base entry of
the stock kernel's adaptive MIPI table for this sensor and 897 MHz is
one of its alternates.

The pixel rate for the timing registers is 840 Mpixel/s: line length
times frame length times frame rate gives that figure in every stock
mode, and the VT PLL (24 MHz / 4 * 210) is the same in all of them.

The controls are exposure (2 lines up to frame length - 10), analogue
gain (codes 0 to 896, gain = 1024 / (1024 - code), up to 8x, as the stock
gain code computes it), digital gain (Q8, 0x100 to 0xfff), vblank
(stock's frame length or longer), read-only hblank, pixel rate and link
frequency, and the SMIA/CCS test pattern at 0x0600 with its four colour
registers. There are no flip controls: stock never writes the
orientation register, so the Bayer order under flips is unknown.

The full-field list turns on the sensor's HDR mode (0x0220 = 0x61) and
sets the second exposure (0x0224) equal to the first. In that mode the
driver writes exposure and analogue gain to both register sets, so the
frame stays uniform.

The media bus code is SGRBG10. The stock module gives CFA code 2 for
every mode. The IMX258 module gives 3, and the IMX258 runs unflipped on
stock, which mainline's imx258 driver reports as RGGB. In the order
BGGR, GBRG, GRBG, RGGB that makes 2 GRBG. The colour bar test pattern
shows whether that holds.

Power-up follows stock: VANA, VIF, VDIG and MCLK 1 ms apart, XCLR
released 1 ms later, then 10 ms before the first access. The init list
programs EXCK for 24 MHz, so probe rejects any other clock rate.

